From eca27dac54e3d515697e3b9b20fcd5bf7c626883 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "tryingET (AK6889)" <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 09:12:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Interpreter: opt-in page images for OpenAI-compatible
 providers

Adds a per-model 'Send page images' setting. When enabled and the provider
uses the default OpenAI-compatible request format, up to 4 images linked in
the page content are fetched by the extension (credentials omitted; png,
jpeg, webp or gif; at most 2 MiB; at least 16x16 px; SVG skipped) and sent
as base64 data URLs in image_url parts of the prompt message. Other
provider formats and models without the setting keep sending text only.

Image links come from the '{{content}}' template variable; note that
handleInterpreterUI's existing variables.content lookup is always empty
because variables are keyed '{{name}}'.
